{#
   Rust module index (`mod.rs`) for a generated state machine directory.

   It exists because Rust resolves a sibling module through its parent
   `mod.rs`, unlike C++ (`-I`) or Kotlin (package path). The file is a
   generated artifact and carries the drift header, so the traceability
   contract requires it to carry an SCE-MAP marker as well.

   The marker names the machine symbol, at the machine's own source
   location. It renders through `_macros/sce_map_marker.jinja2` like
   every other marker in the tree: a hand-written marker string in the
   emitter is a second copy of the shape AND a second copy of the
   location, and the copy that lived here drifted — it cited line 1
   unconditionally, which is the XML declaration, not the `<scxml>`
   element the `_machine` symbol resolves to.
#}
{%- import '_macros/sce_map_marker.jinja2' as sce_map -%}
